\f0\fs24 \cf0 DRAFTING NOTES -- Chip escalates issues with Sarah & Hayley (spec settled 2026-08-07/09; sources: artefacts/review-response/part5.md, arc-tracker/chip-stockwell.md, arc-tracker/hayley-investigates-eloise.md)\
\
WHAT THIS SCENE PAYS AND OPENS\
- Pays Chip's exit line from "Gyges disc pentagram configuration": "I need to talk with Ms Jacobson." That line is currently a promise the manuscript never keeps.\
- Opens the Hayley-investigates-Eloise thread. Payoff in Part 6 is MANDATORY (author): opening it and not landing it would be worse than never opening it. It needs at least one Part 6 beat of Hayley visibly working, or the result reads as authorial convenience.\
- Fixes Part 5's standing problem: Sarah reacting rather than deciding. This is her one decision that costs her something.\
\
BEAT GUIDANCE\
- Chip is an engineer, not a Cassandra. The concession (more discs at lower revolutions could be the safer configuration) is what keeps his credibility -- he offers containment engineering, not doom. Rotherhithe Stasis Collapse is his precedent.\
- The restriction: one or two sentences, no more. Chip cannot leave the Sublime Point compound; Eloise frames it as probably better for him. He is not confined to his quarters and still works. Keep it to that \'97 it covers the delay since his exit line and his absence for the rest of Part 5, and nothing else.\
- Sarah's call: containment is the objective. They believe Johnny and the Sages are managing containment on their own despite themselves. The reader knows this is exactly wrong -- the Sages are accelerating, Johnny is escalating. Dramatic irony is the mode; do not soften it with hedging internalisation.\
- HELD-DOOR BEAT: Sarah's admission (pregnancy degrading judgement and attention) must be written so the reader feels a second, larger admission being withheld behind it -- a door held shut, not absent. Do NOT name what is behind it.\
- CANON FENCE (sarahs-biology): no descent confirmation, no origin leak. Sarah is NOT a Hardy descendant; the descent reading is misdirection that protects the real reveal (the lab, the mother, the test case). Nothing in this scene may confirm or deny.\
\
WHAT NOT TO INHERIT\
- Do not import symptoms from the KB. The timeline's claims for the later medical (all-day nausea, dangerous blood pressure, "well past 15 weeks") are FLAGGED as unsupported by that scene's prose -- Sarah there says she has never been sick and feels healthier than ever. Her state in THIS scene is to be established in drafting: the degradation shows as judgement and attention (and perhaps self-deception about it), not as clinical symptoms.\
\
POSITION AND AFTERMATH\
- Placement (author, 2026-08-09): chapter "Chip complains", between the Jones jukebox chapter ("The Devil in His Ties") and the Tony penthouse chapter ("How Fake Thou Art"). Story-time sits months before the 10 Nov festival -- Hayley gets a long quiet runway before the Part 6 payoff.\
- Every later scene seating Sarah, Hayley and Kathy together (the High Elvis's summons, the intervention, the festival platform) now carries the compact as live subtext. Kathy's own secret (lying to Eloise about the SARA readouts) runs parallel: three of the four women Eloise gathered are independently withholding from her, none knowing the others are.\
- This is Chip's last Part 5 appearance. Next beat: "Chip vs Johnny" (Part 6) -- he fails to stop Johnny, exactly as the Sages planned. His arc is a tragedy of correct warnings delivered at the wrong seniority; the containment agreement here is the mechanism of that failure, not a lapse in it.\
